.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T12:11:35-07:00","id":1448611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448607#post1448607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A touchstone is an anchor that gives you a reason to keep going and anchors your soul/sense of self while the beast tries to gnaw on it like a flimsy chew toy. At least, that's how I interpreted it.<br /> My personal opinion is that I think something is lost when you narrow the selection to people. It's something personal and complex reduced to something too restrictive and simple and it should be about the pc as an individual. A human being is not going to work for everyone, and it's certainly not going to for those vampires whose paths disregard humans altogether - or outright forbid interaction..<br /> <br /> Even if our attachments start with people, they evolve or transfer to things. A ring is important because it belonged to your grandmother, who raised you. A song on the radio reminds you of your best friend when you were a child, and you still looked forward to the future. Your grandmother died last year and haven't seen that friend since you were twelve, but that doesn't mean your time together stopped mattering.<br /> <br /> And like your graveyard touchstone (which sounds like fun), we attach to and gain meaning from things that aren't people.<br /> <br /> There are suicidal people who hang on for the sake of their pets, or even because they want to know how their favourite show ends.<br /> <br /> Places. An environmentalist in life has the local park for a touchstone, they make sure the nature within is protected and that gives their existence a purpose.<br /> <br /> Nightly rituals.A vampire identifies with their comunity. He patrols the neighbourhood, takes up litter picking and generally dedicates an hour every night doing the rounds in his neighbourhood making life better there (or trying, at least). One vampire rereads her favourite book, the one that kept her company when real humans refused.<br /> <br /> A member of an endangered or dead culture takes strength and meaning from keeping it alive in a way that only an immortal can. Maybe their touchstone is a place, object, ritualised activity or job position based around that?<br /> <br /> Religous vampires may treasure their faith, a feeling that when genuine can be extremely strong. They're attached to an object of religious significance. Juzu beads worn with frequent use, a pocket bible bookmarked with favourite passages. A Jewish vampire fights off torpor on Sundays to observe the Sabbath. A muslim vampire gets up every day for prayer.<br /> Or, since this is VtM, change the above to something relevant to the Noddists or Set or something.<br /> <br /> A vampire who's too old to remember what it was like to be human probably can't relate to a mortal, but they might find the middle ground in a fledgling or a young neonate.<br /> The other non-humans might work in a fucked up way... though I would definitely rule out a Garou... Although now that I think on it, a vampire with a werewolf as a touchstone sounds absolutely fucking hilarious, if <i>incredibly </i>short lived.<br /> <br /> So anyway, other things touchstones could be, in my opinion: nightly rituals, songs, specific stories, jobs, objects, places, animals...<br /> Hell, how about a plant? I know somebody who's kept a plant alive for over fifty years because they took it as a cutting from the garden it came from, and that garden had special meaning to them. It's amazing what you can latch onto.<br /> <br /> To me more variety is more interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also really think that despite the books suggesting using them for drama, that touchstones should be treated as the opposite for most of the time. While there certainly will be dangers and conflicts, it's primarily a way to inject brief moments of meaning and possibly peace and happiness into a miserable, nihilistic setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, although I do love the idea of getting Beast Marks for using non-human touchstones. I like the idea that by clinging to something other than humanity to stave off the &quot;beast&quot;, you become noticeably alien, just a sapient version of alien. It's fun to roleplay. And it helps with balance, as, for example, my graveyard is easier to keep functional than a human is to keep alive. I mostly just need to pick up crackpipes and wash off graffiti, and make a few deals so other vampires don't trash the place. It's not easy, but compared to a human who can die to one stray bullet, it's practicably adamantium. So I can not praise the Long Road Out Of Hell people enough for coming up with this mechanic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T14:10:01-07:00","id":1448622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448591#post1448591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You keep saying that but I don't see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Do we need to do this, again? How many threads about Touchstones are we going to have where we need to post/link to a post of all the places V5 Core says this? Can you just, please, for the love of the forums, accept this is an actual flaw in the books in a fashion that lasts more than one thread?<br /> <br /> You have great ideas about how to make Touchstones more engaging, and you completely hamper the ability to show people how to do so when you make it sound like the book itself isn't part of the problem.<br /> <br /> Even if you honestly never see the book that way, take a hint from the rather large number of people (even very pro-V5 people!) that do, and recognize that it might not be a problem for you, but it is a real problem, it comes from a real source, and it needs addressing in a more comprehensive way than, &quot;it would be more fun if you just read things the way I read things.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448594#post1448594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">small thing: you don't recover aggrevated willpower damage by being with your touchstone, you need to do something significant to your touchstone's benefit. there is no reward for just spending time with your touchstone.<br /> <br /> it's not just presentation it's also the mechanics of touchstones that are at fault here</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually just thinking of a way to get the players more involved with Touchstones, and especially a way that encourages interaction with Touchstones, and justifies a bias towards having at least some human ones:<br /> <br /> Emotionally unburdening yourself through a Touchstone reduces your current Stains by 1 (cannot reduce to zero).<br /> <br /> First, this eliminates a lot of the need for them to be &quot;forced&quot; into the drama. If a vampire wants to get some help from a Touchstone in this regard, it means bringing that Touchstone into the grey area between ignorance and being part of the shadows. The Touchstones is going to learn things, know secrets, and even if in the dark about it being all about vampires, has to know that you're in some really bad shit. Instead of the big deal with Touchstones being attacked because it's an easy way for other vampires to drag you down (not that this goes away completely), the political machinations of vampires means they're far more useful alive and well... and unwitting sources of information about you to your political enemies.<br /> <br /> Second, it's another reason to seek out interaction, so PCs are more likely to seek it (and one that doesn't have another real option besides your Remorse checks), and advocate for their Touchstones not disappearing into the background. It's also harder to meaningfully unburden yourself to an empty building that can't respond to whatever you're admitting to doing. Confessing to a priest is a much more significant deal than confessing to an empty box that a priest used to sit in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T14:15:25-07:00","id":1448624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448610#post1448610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have to be unchanging about what makes them remind you of your Humanity. Yes, the book left a lot of leeway to do them horrifically. They also left them a lot of ways to do them straight heroically or uplifting too.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they didn't, or they utterly failed to convey that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T14:31:38-07:00","id":1448627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448624#post1448624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they didn't, or they utterly failed to convey that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as an example, the element of your Conviction can be, &quot;Do not harm Good People&quot; and what inspires you about that person is they are good.<br /> <br /> The only that would damage said Touchstone is that they are either killed or harmed or they become bad people.<br /> <br /> The Touchstone changing is that they no longer embody what you draw strength from. Its not that they start wearing pants instead of dresses. At least that was my interpretation of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T16:09:27-07:00","id":1448630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448627#post1448627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only that would damage said Touchstone is that they are either killed or harmed or they become bad people.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's damage and destroy. You're conflating them. If your Touchstone supports &quot;Do not harm good people,&quot; by being a good person in the eyes of your character:<br /> <br /> 1) Anything that the Touchstone does that tarnishes but doesn't break their image as a good person (hey, humans are flawed), they're damaged.<br /> 2) Anything that completely wrecks the vampire's image of the Touchstone results in it being destroyed.<br /> <br /> Of course, that means in play, you and your ST need a very solid mutual understanding of what &quot;good&quot; means for your vampire. Which is part of the problem with human Touchstones in the circumstances of the OP's post. Some people are hard absolutists and if they see their Touchstone steal, that Touchstone isn't a good person, and is destroyed. Some people are soft absolutists or relativists where stealing can be excused in specific circumstances and it would just damage the Touchstone instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Touchstone changing is that they no longer embody what you draw strength from. Its not that they start wearing pants instead of dresses. At least that was my interpretation of it. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the issue is them changing from the ideal image of them in the vampire's head. Fashion changes may or may not count depending on the specifics (just like the athlete changing teams thing, even trivial things to many people can be vital parts of other people's identities).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T16:33:33-07:00","id":1448631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448630#post1448630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the issue is them changing from the ideal image of them in the vampire's head. Fashion changes may or may not count depending on the specifics (just like the athlete changing teams thing, even trivial things to many people can be vital parts of other people's identities).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually what I see as the biggest appeal of Touchstones. The game is obviously going out of their way to avoid &quot;Bellafication&quot; of Touchstones. They want to be able to make a human friendly mortal that is a genuine source of Humanity and hope to vampires like Doctor Lambert in FOREVER KNIGHT but they also want to avoid making them something that takes away from the personal horror inherently so there's also &quot;crazy stalker&quot; options with Touchstones. This is partially due to the fact that Humanity is no longer completely about being a good person but how well you're holding the Beast at bay.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of horror potential but I think primarily the EVIL STALKER Vampire is meant to be NPCs while more traditional &quot;human friends makes you less of a monster&quot; is meant to be the way PCs are done.<br /> <br /> I think the book just assumes you know how to have a mortal that is NOT in a horrifying relationship with a vampire. There are examples also of it not being terrible.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MoralityPet\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MoralityPet</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T17:09:10-07:00","id":1448635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones#post1448574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But maybe this is all just me. Maybe I keep getting ST's on roll20 who are bad at integrating human touchstones. What is your experience with human touchstones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really positive. I've found Touchstones (when done well) to be compelling characters who add a literally human element to chronicles, provide contrast to the Kindred politics, can hammer home the personal horror of being a vampire, can have some really heartwarming scenes, etc. Two of my game's current PCs have probably spent as much time roleplaying with their Touchstones as they have with any (individual) vampire. <br /> <br /> Mind, it's taken some trial and error. When I first started using Touchstones (with Requiem 2e), around the time I first got into playing the WoD, they fell victim to the same &quot;but they never come up in-game and are irrelevant to the chronicle's actual story&quot; problem you're describing. I had to make a deliberate effort to use them better. It's paid off. <br /> <br /> I also <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443448-tips-for-running-touchstones\">made a thread</a> a monthish ago on ways GMs can keep Touchstones interesting and story-relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T17:19:30-07:00","id":1448637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448627#post1448627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just as an example, the element of your Conviction can be, &amp;quot;Do not harm Good People&amp;quot; and what inspires you about that person is they are good.<br /> <br /> The only that would damage said Touchstone is that they are either killed or harmed or they become bad people.<br /> <br /> The Touchstone changing is that they no longer embody what you draw strength from. Its not that they start wearing pants instead of dresses. At least that was my interpretation of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... How about a mechanic where instead of the touchstone being destroyed, a vampire has a chance to overcome the static nature of vampirism, self reflect and try to use their humanity to empathize with the touchstone?<br /> <br /> If they're successful they can adapt their convictions to the change in the touchstone and keep them, growing as a person with them <br /> <br /> &quot;Do not harm Good People, but accept and forgive that everyone struggles with doing the right thing&quot;?<br /> <br /> Or flat out replace it with a new one, like &quot;Accept change&quot;? &quot;There is no such thing as a Good Person&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T17:19:55-07:00","id":1448638,"title":"","content":"I think you're speaking a bit for what some people involved with V5 like to do with things instead of what the books tell STs and players to do with them.<br /> <br /> Even so, as noted, the rules are lacking to actually get to the game-play objectives you're talking about. Hence my suggestion about things like having more rewards for direct interaction with your Touchstones that actually help you maintain your Humanity, instead of only the indirect way that having a Touchstone relates to a Conviction, that only really matters if you're violating Chronicle Tenets.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure Dr. Lambert is really a great example for getting away from &quot;Bellafiction,&quot; because she's really not that different of a character from Bella Swan. It's just less grating because (a) she's better written, (b) she's an adult and deals with romance in a mature fashion instead of being an idiot teen, (c) and the story actually takes time developing the relationship.<br /> <br /> Forever Knight's has plenty of romantic angst about the vampire and human resolving their emotions, the vampire's enemies using her against him, and all that stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T17:25:37-07:00","id":1448640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448631#post1448631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of horror potential but I think primarily the EVIL STALKER Vampire is meant to be NPCs while more traditional &quot;human friends makes you less of a monster&quot; is meant to be the way PCs are done.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue is the V5 rulebook does not do a very good job at conveying that. One of the principle examples I remember from it is a Touchstone getting abducted by rivals, so the vampire PC rescues them, then makes them drink poison so that can never happen again. <br /> <br /> Just... sets a bad example. If that's the typical Touchstone experience, it's not a good way to get new players to care about Touchstones. Many players are not going to want to emotionally invest themselves in a character who the rulebook says adversaries will use against you and even your own PC may want to kill, because they are better off dead.<br /> <br /> The Requiem 2e rulebook was much better at providing examples of cool, interesting, and heart-tugging Touchstones I'd want to use in a game, and without any of the &quot;they are liabilities that enemies will use against you&quot; baggage attached. The book put more emphasis on the personal relationship between the vampire and the Touchstone and the ways in which being a vampire caused dramatic complications. <br /> <br /> Interestingly, I didn't think any personal horror was lost. If anything, Requiem 2e did it <i>better</i> than V5 did. <br /> <br /> (Then again, the Requiem 2e rulebook had some top-notch writing by the amazingly talented Rose Bailey...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T17:36:33-07:00","id":1448642,"title":"","content":"VtR 2e also recognized from the get go that non-human Touchstones should be a thing even if rare in young vampires that still have living connections to their human lives.<br /> <br /> Something I think that gets forgotten in RPG design sometimes, is that sometimes saying that you can do something uncommon (and I don't mean the Golden Rule, I mean actually having support for it in the system) actually gets people to do what you present as average more frequently. Even aside from Touchstones, when CofD 2e took away the &quot;5 dots cost double at creation,&quot; didn't lead to a glut of characters with 5s in stuff (yes the change in XP helped). Telling the ST to trust their players, the book creates a better atmosphere for players to make organic characters.<br /> <br /> There's a reason some of us really think V5's examples, and comments about what &quot;good&quot; STs should be doing are so detrimental. They focus the players are fearing ST actions, instead of reassuring them that the book is telling the ST to trust the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T19:03:47-07:00","id":1448646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448642#post1448642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I think that gets forgotten in RPG design sometimes, is that sometimes saying that you can do something uncommon (and I don't mean the Golden Rule, I mean actually having support for it in the system)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall any references to the Golden Rule in VtR 2e. There might have been the usual &quot;rules facilitate story, story comes first&quot; caveat at the start of one of the mechanics chapters (I think? It's been a while), but by and large, I got the impression the game trusted its own mechanics more and trusted them to facilitate the kinds of narratives it wanted to tell.<br /> <br /> I don't think the VtR 2e mechanics were without flaws, but coincidentally, I like its mechanics more than V5's too.<br /> <br /> The book just came off as much more confident in itself and confident in the people who were playing it. It didn't feel like it was &quot;trying as hard.&quot; As you say, there was more emphasis on the ST trusting players than players fearing the ST. It also didn't hurt that players were encouraged to embrace adversity by means of carrots (i.e., the Conditions system, taking Beats to downgrade failures to botches). <br /> <br /> Maybe some of the book's &quot;confidence&quot; can be chalked up to the history and context behind the games. V5 had enormous pressure to bring one of the most successful RPGs of all time into the 21st century, while also tapping into the nostalgia factor behind why it was so popular in the '90s. VtR was more obscure, the devs had accepted it would stay that way, and they simply wanted to bring the second edition fully out from under the shadow of Masquerade to be its own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T20:32:39-07:00","id":1448649,"title":"","content":"VtR 2e's confidence is there, but it is built on a lot of hard fought experience from the lack of confidence in VtR 1e. VtR 1e, like V5, was in a fairly tough situation. It was the game WW killed VtM for. The TTRPG bubble had burst, but WW was still seen as one of the major RPG companies after accounting for WotC. It was going to make a new Vampire for a new generation without tossing out everything the old fans loved. VtR 1e had a lot of flaws from its own choices in that position.<br /> <br /> A lot of early CofD 2e freelancers have talked about how much the freedom to design more towards trusting the ST and players to want to play the game, and thus focus on giving them the tools to do so rather than the futility of writing rules that were made to either curtail &quot;bad&quot; players or enforce ST authority through the rules saying so.<br /> <br /> It's just a shame V5 didn't take that feeling from VtR 2e when pulling inspiration from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T21:44:56-07:00","id":1448653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448649#post1448649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtR 2e's confidence is there, but it is built on a lot of hard fought experience from the lack of confidence in VtR 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtR 1e is Revised-era Masquerade with the serial numbers filed off. I can enjoy it quite a lot for what it is. Some of the books, like Ghouls and Nomads, are really good. But you can see how hard it tries to not be Masquerade (&quot;vampires do not <b>ever</b> communicate across cities! The Fog of Eternity steals <b>all</b> your memories!&quot;), and comes off as scared of accidentally turning into its predecessor.<br /> <br /> It's telling that 2e manages to relax many of those &quot;anti-Masquerade&quot; ideas while feeling like a more distinct setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's just a shame V5 didn't take that feeling from VtR 2e when pulling inspiration from it. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure they could have. They were designing a game that, like VtR 1e, was trying to define itself against its predecessor rather than to be its own thing.<br /> <br /> It also didn't help that lots of the writers/developers for V5 were also either new to publishing WoD books or hadn't done so in years and years. VtR 2e had its share of relatively newbie writers, but I feel like it had a solid crew of senior people (Rose Bailey, Olivia Hill, Filamena Young, David Brookshaw, Stewart Wilson, et al) who'd worked on WoD/CofD books before, worked together before, and were working for a company that had published lots of books before. All of that was gone with V5. &quot;White Wolf&quot; was a brand new company under an old name.<br /> <br /> VtR 2e had only a single developer, too. Rose Bailey. Her voice dominates the book. V5's corebook had an entire <i>ten</i> developers; in fact, the exact same people as its authors list, and its concept and design list.<br /> <br /> VtR 2e was just a much sleeker, polished, focused, confident product. And I'm saying this as someone who prefers Masquerade's setting over Requiem's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T02:41:47-07:00","id":1448669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448594#post1448594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">small thing: you don't recover aggrevated willpower damage by being with your touchstone, you need to do something significant to your touchstone's benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but it's much easier to do something which benefits them if you are near them and/or know what would benefit them. If you never see them or interact with them, it'll be quite hard to help them.<br /> <br /> That said, I do like Heavy Arms idea, although to really work I think it might require moving when Remorse Checks happen, as there will often not be time to unburden oneself on a Touchstone before the end of a Session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26420-desparen","name":"Desparen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T05:48:26-07:00","id":1448677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Desparen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448669#post1448669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know, but it's much easier to do something which benefits them if you are near them and/or know what would benefit them. If you never see them or interact with them, it'll be quite hard to help them.</div> </div> </div> </div>the problem there is then that you're maintaining a relationship so you could do something significant to aid them to recover agg wp damage or you could recover agg wp damage by doing something significant to further your own agenda which usually brings additional benefits(because you're doing something to your own benefit). which means that not only is it harder to recover wp through touchstones (because you need to maintain a relationship on top of doing something significant), you also gain less from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T06:08:21-07:00","id":1448679,"title":"","content":"I don't think original VtR touchstones are supposed to be integrated into the story. Rather, the vampire consorts with them <i>in spite</i> of their night to night business, which gives them a human perspective on existence and their condition, instead of doing vampire things and thinking vampire thoughts every waking hour. They remind them that they're more than what their hunger and kindred society demands they be.<br /> <br /> VtM is different from that, because its vampires don't have to address human needs to remain as functional beings; they just have to establish a set of principles and commit to them. A graveyard, where a Hecata probably works anyway, isn't likely to ground them in the way that a person can, but it could help them focus on what they aspire to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T06:41:24-07:00","id":1448681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448679#post1448679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtM is different from that, because its vampires don't have to address human needs to remain as functional beings; they just have to establish a set of principles and commit to them. A graveyard, where a Hecata probably works anyway, isn't likely to ground them in the way that a person can, but it could help them focus on what they aspire to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the graveyard is to reinforce a Feral Heart conviction: &quot;you and your Pack are one. Protect them at all costs.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T12:55:52-07:00","id":1448711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448679#post1448679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think original VtR touchstones are supposed to be integrated into the story. Rather, the vampire consorts with them <i>in spite</i> of their night to night business, which gives them a human perspective on existence and their condition, instead of doing vampire things and thinking vampire thoughts every waking hour. They remind them that they're more than what their hunger and kindred society demands they be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure this tracks. Touchstones are part of a Requiem vampire's night to night business; not just the vampire politics and power playing part of it. Requiem comes off very much as wanting Touchstones to be part of the story, because the struggle between the demands of vampire society and the efforts to maintain Humanity is supposed to be a central thematic struggle.<br /> <br /> Requiem Touchstones aren't necessarily going to be constant on-screen presences (unless you opt to make them so with additional Merits) that are working side-by-side with the PCs on most activities, but they are clearly supposed to be characters that come up as part of the story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T14:01:57-07:00","id":1448715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448711#post1448711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not really sure this tracks. Touchstones are part of a Requiem vampire's night to night business; not just the vampire politics and power playing part of it. Requiem comes off very much as wanting Touchstones to be part of the story, because the struggle between the demands of vampire society and the efforts to maintain Humanity is supposed to be a central thematic struggle.<br /> <br /> Requiem Touchstones aren't necessarily going to be constant on-screen presences (unless you opt to make them so with additional Merits) that are working side-by-side with the PCs on most activities, but they are clearly supposed to be characters that come up as part of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rough and weird way to think about Touchstones, their akin to Home Improvement's Mr. Wilson in a way-You get into the action and mess of being a vampire, and then you have this person who may not ever be involved directly with the plot, but has an essential perspective to how your struggle, and in particular an element that's been/is now missing in your life*, and the interactions you have with them are primarily to help you reorganize your points of value and perspective on the problems. There's a lot of other narratives that include this sort of dynamic and characters for this person-a end-of-second-act-, beginning-of-third-act perspective bringer who allows you to confront both the conflict and self with the thematic focus.<br /> <br /> Where this breaks down, of course, is also in the interaction-Wilson knew pretty much everything going on in TIm's life, where as things an get <i>lost</i> if a Touchstone is brought too much into a vampires primary life.<br /> <br /> Regardless, touchstones are both there for downbeat scenes (sequels, if we wanna use the technical term) to have your character reorient, and for ramping up tension(any scene risking the touchstone inherently raises the stakes).<br /> <br /> *In the case of Tim, we could summarize it as &quot;a more positive masculinity&quot;-empathy, patience, nuance, humility, etc., in the case of touchstones, it's Humanity (and what that means to both the touchstone and the vampire).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T03:18:02-07:00","id":1448766,"title":"","content":"I have seen touchstones working very well, but most of the time they fall to the wayside.<br /> <br /> I feel like touchstones need 1. a lot of work 2. ST and Players NEED to be on the same wavelength.<br /> <br /> After a couple tries I would only use it again with players I already know and trust or by baby steps very slowly.<br /> <br /> The book would have been better in my opinion by pointing towards non human touchstones, giving more advice for a simple start, and pointing out positive ways for interaction. Maybe even put it into a section called advanced options (I also put humors there).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","user":"mfalkenb","date":". 05-17-2021, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T06:04:26-07:00","id":1448769,"title":"","content":"Not a fan of touchstones in any form, but I can see how they could be useful if you wanted to run a very specific type of game. I just have no interest in that type of game at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448653#post1448653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> VtR 1e is Revised-era Masquerade with the serial numbers filed off.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's more like swapping out everything except the lower register of a full auto AR15 and then changing the trigger out for a semi-auto only one. And then filing 1/2 the serial number off. There are far more differences than similarities in the two and VtR's 8+ standard difficulty vs VtM 6+ standard is a very noticeable change. Also VtR is considered CofD not WoD.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for how to use touchstones in V5 the book says :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\"><b>Of course, any Storyteller worth their salt </b>creates story and </span><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">drama that puts pressure on the player to decide between harming </span><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">their Touchstone and achieving </span><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">some vampiric goal. </span> </div> </div> </div> -V5 page 240<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sounds like the rules wanting to covey touchstones should be used a certain way to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T10:56:21-07:00","id":1448787,"title":"","content":"Touchstones are great as long as they are OPTIONAL like in Requiem<br /> <br /> While sometimes you want to make a gritty story , 99% of the games are urban fantasy full of politics , adding up to 4 extra characters with no relation to the plot is derailment","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T17:16:58-07:00","id":1448819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448787#post1448787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touchstones are great as long as they are OPTIONAL like in Requiem<br /> <br /> While sometimes you want to make a gritty story , 99% of the games are urban fantasy full of politics , adding up to 4 extra characters with no relation to the plot is derailment</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think if they made Masquerade touchstones more flexible like Requiem touchstone they\u2019ll be more liked? Like being able to keep a stable of horses that remind you of your horse breeding days when you where alive, or maybe a portrait of yourself in a museum that you love that people look at it . But other Kindred don\u2019t want a person in a 300 year old portrait that they can see walking around.<br /> <br /> Vampire 5 edition kind of uses what Requiem pioneered in the Masquerade IP, plus some other huge changes compared to earlier storytelling systems . And yeah I understand why it\u2019s divisive but let\u2019s not turn this thread into a edition war","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T02:17:03-07:00","id":1448836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448819#post1448819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think if they made Masquerade touchstones more flexible like Requiem touchstone they\u2019ll be more liked? Like being able to keep a stable of horses that remind you of your horse breeding days when you where alive, or maybe a portrait of yourself in a museum that you love that people look at it . But other Kindred don\u2019t want a person in a 300 year old portrait that they can see walking around.<br /> <br /> Vampire 5 edition kind of uses what Requiem pioneered in the Masquerade IP, plus some other huge changes compared to earlier storytelling systems . And yeah I understand why it\u2019s divisive but let\u2019s not turn this thread into a edition war</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i think it's less an issue of flexibility then of purpose. in V5 touchstone are obsessions, bastions of virtue in the eyes of a vampire that are to be idolized and emulated but forgotten the second they die or betray the image the vampire has of them. and most ppl don't want that, it also doesn't make sense for alot of character concepts to have such an obsession with a person.<br /> <br /> i think the reason ppl ask for more flexible touchstones is because the easiest way to fix this issue with homebrewing is by broadening what you can be obsessed with thereby broadening the types of obsessions you can have.<br /> <br /> while increased flexibility is a solution, i don't think it's the best solution and definitly not the solution they should aim for for a theoretical V5 revised","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T04:52:29-07:00","id":1448842,"title":"","content":"I feel v5 does too much to shift vampires in the direction of analogues for a persecuted, mentally ill minority. (persecuted; The transition of focus towards the SI and thus big goverment as a threat. Mentally ill: Messy criticals) You might like that if you fit the bill or you have a very specific idea of vampires, but for a neurotypical individual with fair social skills, or perhaps someone who liked the idea of vampires being suave political predators, it's a bit frustrating to be shoehorned into this narrow scope of what V5 thinks a vampire should be; Touchstones are just fucking weird. No healthy mind affixes their own convictions to a few individuals, and loses their grasp on their convictions when that person changes or is hurt. How can I play a self-assured political predator when I need my romanticised Bella swans? How can I run a satire of monsters when everyone needs a human to keep them human? <br /> <br /> Part of what made Vampire great is that you could play any kind of Vampire. You can play a crazy vampire, a sane vampire, a sexy vampire, a hideous vampire, someone who cares or someone who does not, A saint or a sinner.. In V5 I absolutely have to be maladjusted vampire, a creep, a weirdo, &quot;what the hell am I doing here&quot; kind of vampire; it's mechanically ordained and gilded by fluff: I have to fear messy criticals, I have to fear someone harming the fellow I need to stalk, only the golden rule can save me from this damnation, but how much do we want to rely on that golden rule eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T05:24:33-07:00","id":1448844,"title":"","content":"My view of touchstones is rather mixed, because I loathe human touchstones, but adore my non-human touchstones and their resultant Beast Marks. In every game where I've been allowed to use the Long Road Out Of Hell hombrew: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N7z5WJa4WcghanB-mSGqdqIymRB7vteu/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N7z...ymRB7vteu/view</a> I've had an absolute blast interacting with my non-human touchstones and roleplaying my Beast Marks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T05:55:32-07:00","id":1448847,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about something regarding experiences:<br /> <br /> Something I was thinking about when coming up with examples of Touchstones in VtM and VtR games I've been in before the Touchstone concept was even introduced lead me to a realization. The vast majority of examples that really clicked were games where there was significant time playing pre-Embrace. Whether just extended preludes, or even really playing mortals for awhile before the PCs got Embraced, humans that they fledgling vampires cared about were abundant, and already well established characters in the game.... because they were NPCs that were already part of the story, ones the PCs had already formed bonds with, and ones the players had already developed interest in keeping around. <br /> <br /> The other examples that came to mind were ones players brought to the table and were already planning on having via Backgrounds or whatnot anyway.<br /> <br /> I think this hits on a weakness in human touchstones, and somewhat why VtR 2e's approach tends to sit better: When you <b>have</b> to make them, they don't feel organic. They feel tacked on. You're not making a big deal about your college buddy, or your mortal family, or whatever because you wanted them specifically, but because you had to come up with some ideas and you're looking for things to hook them into. In VtR 2e, yeah you have to define one Touchstone, but more (and more is good to have) is something you can just let happen in-game. Whether your character is looking for them, or happens across them, that organic experience makes them more appealing. When V5 basically says, &quot;make 3, that's what you get,&quot; I think it can rub people the wrong way because they don't get the real chance to develop why those Touchstones exist by playing their characters.<br /> <br /> Do people feel like that might be part of the issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T06:08:07-07:00","id":1448848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448847#post1448847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about something regarding experiences:<br /> <br /> Something I was thinking about when coming up with examples of Touchstones in VtM and VtR games I've been in before the Touchstone concept was even introduced lead me to a realization. The vast majority of examples that really clicked were games where there was significant time playing pre-Embrace. Whether just extended preludes, or even really playing mortals for awhile before the PCs got Embraced, humans that they fledgling vampires cared about were abundant, and already well established characters in the game.... because they were NPCs that were already part of the story, ones the PCs had already formed bonds with, and ones the players had already developed interest in keeping around.<br /> <br /> The other examples that came to mind were ones players brought to the table and were already planning on having via Backgrounds or whatnot anyway.<br /> <br /> I think this hits on a weakness in human touchstones, and somewhat why VtR 2e's approach tends to sit better: When you <b>have</b> to make them, they don't feel organic. They feel tacked on. You're not making a big deal about your college buddy, or your mortal family, or whatever because you wanted them specifically, but because you had to come up with some ideas and you're looking for things to hook them into. In VtR 2e, yeah you have to define one Touchstone, but more (and more is good to have) is something you can just let happen in-game. Whether your character is looking for them, or happens across them, that organic experience makes them more appealing. When V5 basically says, &quot;make 3, that's what you get,&quot; I think it can rub people the wrong way because they don't get the real chance to develop why those Touchstones exist by playing their characters.<br /> <br /> Do people feel like that might be part of the issue?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i think that comes down more that neither system gives you a reason to want to develop a relationship with a touchstone the diffrence being that if you don't want to develop a relation with a touchstone in requim that's fine because you don't need a touchstonein the first place where as in V5 tough shit you still have to take them.<br /> <br /> if you need the players to take a touchstone then you need to give them a reason to develop a relationship with said touchstone or even want a relationship with said touchstones in the first place.<br /> <br /> well that's not entirely true, they did give a reason: your character is creepily obsessed with them. so really we would need to figure out why ppl don't want to develop a relationship with their touchstone for that specific reason","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 05-18-2021, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T06:47:51-07:00","id":1448852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448574-what-do-you-think-of-human-touchstones?p=1448847#post1448847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you <b>have</b> to make them, they don't feel organic. They feel tacked on. You're not making a big deal about your college buddy, or your mortal family, or whatever because you wanted them specifically, but because you had to come up with some ideas and you're looking for things to hook them into. In VtR 2e, yeah you have to define one Touchstone, but more (and more is good to have) is something you can just let happen in-game. Whether your character is looking for them, or happens across them, that organic experience makes them more appealing. When V5 basically says, &quot;make 3, that's what you get,&quot; I think it can rub people the wrong way because they don't get the real chance to develop why those Touchstones exist by playing their characters.<br /> <br /> Do people feel like that might be part of the issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> Previously we had merits, flaws and backgrounds that covered a character's attachments. &quot;I have, unbeknownst to anyone, told my grandfather what I am and what happened to me. He provdes me shelter and resources, and helps my character cope with the isolation of being a vampire.&quot; Ok, take the Dark Secret flaw and a relevant background.<br /> The player, by voluntarily putting this on the character sheet, wants this to be part of his story. By using the flaw, the character gives the go-ahead for you to endanger his grandfather for drama.<br /> <br /> If the player wants to focus on vampire politics exclusively, we waste time putting stuff down we're not going to use.<br /> By saying the most deeply held ideals and values you gave your character only exist because of some npcs you didn't even want to exist in the first place, you get hostility because they're intruding on somebody's character concept.<br /> <br /> I do think they could work as their own specific mechanic. Touchstones providing a mechanical benefit to represent their positive emotional impact on a vampire's humanity/path rating is worth exploring I think, but as it stands they are way too limiting. I like the concept, but I really think they need a rework.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I find that players love adopting npcs. Especially if it's inconvenient to their ST, When you ask them to come up with a backstory it's humming and hawing and meh. When it's a horribly disfigured feral szlachta or something, oh no, it simply <i>must</i> join the party!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-18-2021, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T08:47:05-07:00","id":1448869,"title":"","content":"I'd say its something that could be useful for some characters but not others, so it would always be case by case. I always think of Dexter and the Code of Harry when I think of this - how he had certain 'rules' he was conditioned to follow to survive and thrive and remain undetected but also to allow him to indulge his nature. In a sense the Code is meant to keep Dexter functional in human society and 'in touch' with his human side. Now while the Code itself is more a 'thing', Harry the person was a significant influence on Dexter and keeping him 'human' so in a sense would be a touchstone. Likewise to be successfully functional in human society interacting with other people (and having connections) is part of staying 'in touch' with the mortal realm. And this is going to sound 'odd' (and perhaps reinforce that idea that 'mental illness' thing someone suggested) but remember that all humans have to be conditioned into certain behaviors, accepted norms and practices, etc. and 'Normal' tends to be defined in those terms. But humans don't really fit into nice neat boxes and many of us resist being pigeonholed in that way so may resist society's pressures to 'normalize' - we're just talking about learned behaviors and the ability (and method) by which people assimilate them. Hell, growing up *I* had to learn different ways to 'learn' because I don't learn like 'normal' people and I struggle in 'normal' life. Doesn't mean I can't function but it required a different approach to what I suppose you can say is 'being human' and yet I can be as normal as most people. In many ways I can function better (I'm more aware of the process for one thing - most people won't think about it because its part of being 'normal'.) <br /> <br /> But as I said everyone is different and the methods by which they learn and adapt will also differ (What works for one won't work for another) and likewise the 'touchstones' that are effective (if any) would also differ. Heck, maybe touchstones aren't the best approach for some characters and something else should be employed. As long as it serves the same purpose it's all good. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}